"""E5 adapter: MUSE (Kim et al., NeurIPS 2024) under the label-free re-evaluation protocol.

Official code: ./src = github.com/kswoo97/GLAD_MUSE @ 07da392034b6c4897a08de658abfb7a61bf09728 (no license
file; unmodified). MUSE's classes and functions are imported from ./src and called as they are; the only
copied code is (i) MUSE_representation_learning.train() (instrumented: evaluate each snapshot when it is
taken, checkpoint/resume), (ii) data_loader.prepare_data() (one fix), (iii) the label-free body of
MUSE_oneclass_classification.train_MLP() and the score line of evaluate_with_Reconstruction(). Every
deviation is marked "# CHANGE" and listed in NOTES.md section 1.6.

Data, folds, held-out split, seeds, metrics, run ids and the per-run JSON "part" schema are those of
evalpaper/harness/run_eval.py (utilities below are copies of that file's helpers; UB-GOLD's loaders
are extracted verbatim from harness/ubgold_src with `ast`, as the harness does).

One run = (MUSE, dataset, fold, hp) with hp in {ubgold, hpfree} (NOTES.md section 1.3):
  * ubgold : MUSE_hyperparameters.pickle entry <key>/anom_0 (released, validation-tuned), or the modal
             released anom_0 configuration for datasets MUSE did not release (COX2, ENZYMES, MUTAG);
  * hpfree : main.py argparse defaults (lr 1e-3, dim 32, n_layers 3, gamma 1.0).
Evaluation point = MUSE snapshot (every 20 of 200 epochs) + MLP autoencoder fitted on the 80 % fit graphs'
error representations at that snapshot (MUSE's own two-stage design). Anomaly score = sum_l (z^_l-z_l)^2/s_l
(negated MUSE normality score). Held-out-normal mean score = VAL-NORMAL signal (A3).

Usage:
  PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1 python -B run_method.py --method MUSE --dataset BZR --fold 0 [--hp hpfree]
